diff -ruN a/gnu/localtime-buffer.c b/gnu/localtime-buffer.c
Fix infinite recursion in rpl_localtime when built against Gnulib time.h.

On Solaris 2.5.1 with GCC 4.x, Gnulib's internal time.h macro-defines 
`localtime` to `rpl_localtime`. When `localtime-buffer.c` executes 
`struct tm *tm = localtime (timep);`, it expands to `rpl_localtime`, 
causing infinite stack recursion and SIGSEGV.

Undefining `localtime` ensures `rpl_localtime` invokes the underlying 
libc `localtime` symbol directly.
It happens while performing a tile test (-t)
--- a/gnu/localtime-buffer.c	2017-12-16 13:23:32.000000000 +0000
+++ b/gnu/localtime-buffer.c	2026-10-06 11:31:01.288295000 +0000
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 
 /* Specification.  */
 #include "localtime-buffer.h"
+#undef localtime
 
 #if GETTIMEOFDAY_CLOBBERS_LOCALTIME || TZSET_CLOBBERS_LOCALTIME
 
